# The build context of demo/Dockerfile is the repository (compose.override.yaml, the CI lanes), read through this list
# alone (BuildKit takes <Dockerfile>.dockerignore over the context's .dockerignore). Nothing is sent but what is named
# here: the demo, the kit's recipes as the demo reads them (each recipe's manifest, README, templates, assets and PHP),
# the root files the gallery reads at run time, and tools/sync-demo, which the production build runs.
*

# the kit as the demo reads it (app.kit_dir: the demo's parent); a recipe's directories are those its copy-files names
!manifest.json
!kit.css
!INSTALL.md
!llms.txt
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!docs/GUIDE.md
!*/manifest.json
!*/README.md
!*/templates/
!*/assets/
!*/src/
!*/config/

# the demo app, without what is installed, built or local to a machine
!demo/
demo/var/
demo/vendor/
demo/public/assets/
demo/public/bundles/
demo/assets/vendor/
demo/tests/
demo/.env.local
demo/.env.local.php
demo/.env.*.local
demo/compose*.yaml
demo/Dockerfile*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# never: tests, the Composer package, node packages, the repository's own files
*/tests/
**/node_modules/
packages/
tests/
.git/
.github/

# copies the recipes into the demo at build time (removed from the production image after)
tools/
!tools/sync-demo
